---
/**
 * Fig. 1 (Document AI) — the packaging decision, drawn as the difference it makes.
 * The claim: the model and its licence are mounted rather than baked into the image,
 * so licence expiry is a swap instead of a rebuild, and the shipped image is far smaller.
 */
---

<figure>
  <div class="figbox">
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 920 300"
      role="img"
      style="min-width:620px"
      aria-label="Left: the naive packaging bakes application code, the recognition model and its licence into one 19 gigabyte image, so licence expiry forces a full rebuild. Right: the shipped design keeps a small application image, layers the model separately, and mounts the licence at run time, giving a 5.28 gigabyte image where licence expiry is a swap."
    >
      <defs>
        <marker id="da-ar" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path class="hlfill" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"></path>
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <g font-size="12" fill="currentColor">
        <text x="30" y="28" opacity="0.72">NAIVE — bake everything in</text>
        <text x="510" y="28" opacity="0.72">SHIPPED — mount what expires</text>

        <line class="grid-line" x1="460" y1="14" x2="460" y2="286" stroke-dasharray="3 5"></line>

        <!-- left: one monolithic image -->
        <rect x="30" y="48" width="330" height="168" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"></rect>
        <text x="42" y="70" font-size="10.5" opacity="0.6">container image</text>

        <rect x="52" y="82" width="286" height="34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.75"></rect>
        <text x="195" y="104" text-anchor="middle">application code</text>

        <rect x="52" y="124" width="286" height="46" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.75"></rect>
        <text x="195" y="152" text-anchor="middle">recognition model</text>

        <rect x="52" y="178" width="286" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.75"></rect>
        <text x="195" y="197" text-anchor="middle">licence</text>

        <text x="195" y="244" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15">19 GB</text>
        <text x="195" y="266" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" opacity="0.62">expiry ⇒ full rebuild</text>

        <!-- right: layered, with the licence outside -->
        <rect x="510" y="48" width="300" height="126" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"></rect>
        <text x="522" y="70" font-size="10.5" opacity="0.6">container image</text>

        <rect x="532" y="82" width="256" height="32" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.75"></rect>
        <text x="660" y="103" text-anchor="middle">application code</text>

        <rect x="532" y="122" width="256" height="40" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.75"></rect>
        <text x="660" y="147" text-anchor="middle">model layer</text>

        <rect class="hl" x="600" y="212" width="120" height="36" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 4"></rect>
        <text class="hl" x="660" y="235" text-anchor="middle">licence</text>

        <line class="hl" x1="660" y1="208" x2="660" y2="180" stroke-width="1.4" marker-end="url(#da-ar)"></line>
        <text class="hl" x="740" y="196" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5">mounted at run time</text>

        <text x="660" y="286" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15">5.28 GB</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <b>Fig. 1 — The licence is mounted, not baked in.</b>
    Keeping the third-party model in its own layer and the licence outside the image
    entirely means renewal is a swap rather than a rebuild-and-redeploy, and drops the
    shipped artifact from 19 GB to 5.28 GB.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
